# Neovim plugin lockfile. lazy.nvim rewrites it on every plugin update, so managing it
# here means routine maintenance leaves the source and the target out of sync until
# someone remembers to re-add it — a diff to reconcile after every update, forever.
#
# The cost is that a fresh provision resolves plugins at install time rather than
# restoring this exact set, so a rebuilt machine can get newer plugins than the one it
# replaced. That is the normal lockfile trade-off, taken deliberately: the file is
# regenerated by lazy.nvim on first launch either way, and the sync friction is daily
# while a rebuild is rare.
.config/nvim/lazy-lock.json

